## Local Agent Configuration
##
## These variables configure the LLM provider and external services used when
## running the agent locally (e.g., the MAF quickstart tutorial).
## They are NOT consumed by MCP server code.
##
## Copy this file to .env.agent and fill in values for your setup.
## See also docs/tutorials/maf_quickstart/.env.example for tutorial-specific guidance.

## === LLM Provider (Azure OpenAI / TRAPI) ===

# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT="https://trapi.research.microsoft.com/gcr/shared"
# AOAI_SCOPE="api://trapi/.default"
# API_VERSION="2025-04-01-preview"
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_NAME="gpt-5.1_2025-11-13"
# MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME="gpt-4o"

## === Azure Foundry / DeepResearch ===

# AZURE_AI_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT="https://agora-research-resource.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/agora-research"
# DEEP_RESEARCH_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME="o3-deep-research"
# BING_RESOURCE_NAME="agorabing"
# BING_GROUNDING_CONNECTION_ID="/subscriptions/7be6291d-d314-4fb5-8377-b89b8b116529/resourceGroups/agora-foundry-rg/providers/Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts/agora-research-resource/projects/agora-research/connections/agorabing"

## === Data Lake (optional, for agent-side artifact search) ===

## Pick ONE backend or leave both unset to skip data lake features.

## Backend A) Azure AI Search-backed catalog (production / shared deployments)
# DATA_LAKE_SEARCH_ENDPOINT="https://agora-ai-search.search.windows.net"
# DATA_LAKE_CATALOG_INDEX_NAME="artifact-registry"
# AZURE_SEARCH_API_KEY="your-search-key-or-leave-unset-for-entra"

## Backend B) Local YAML catalog (no Azure required; BM25 keyword search)
# DATA_LAKE_LOCAL_CATALOG="src/data_lake/tools/adapters/catalog.example.yaml"

## === Alternative LLM Providers ===
## Uncomment one block; see docs/tutorials/maf_quickstart/.env.example for details.

## Azure OpenAI via API key:
# LLM_PROVIDER=azure_openai_apikey
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY="your-api-key"

## OpenAI (api.openai.com):
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."
# OPENAI_MODEL="gpt-4o"

## Ollama (local model server):
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL="http://localhost:11434/v1"
# OLLAMA_MODEL="llama3.1"
